  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3x+\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{x}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3x+\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[3x+\\sqrt{x}]^{\u2032}}{[\\sqrt{x}]^{\u2032}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(3+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})}{\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(6\\sqrt{x}+1) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
